From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 15:30:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] winewayland: Preserve DOOM Eternal's idle Vulkan client surface

DOOM Eternal recreates VkSurfaces along with its HDR swapchains, retaining
references to the old VkSurfaces after their swapchains have been destroyed.
The ref == 1 condition added by the background-presenter isolation patch
prevents the client-surface cache from serving these replacements. Each new
client loses the previous wl_surface's DMA-BUF feedback and replaces its
visible subsurface.

Allow DOOM Eternal to reuse an idle cached client despite those old surface
references. Keep its attachment intact until the regular attach/update path
finds an actual parent or role change. The cache reference transfers to the
new VkSurface as before; old VkSurfaces keep their own references. Never reuse
a client while busy_ref is nonzero.

Keep the existing reference isolation and detach behavior for other programs:
in particular, Purple's independently reusable graphics probes must not alias
its active game presenter. Do not suppress Vulkan out-of-date/suboptimal
results, disable HDR, or change swapchain image counts.

This restores the surface-cache behavior needed by this application, based
on Etaash Mathamsetty's client-surface caching work (508b956d6447). It relies
on the same Mesa WSI object-lifetime support as that existing patch:
https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/34918

The live capture established Wine generation rejection and repeated client
replacement; the effect of this change on HDR flicker still needs a runtime
retest. No game binaries or installed Proton files are modified.
---

diff --git a/dlls/winewayland.drv/vulkan.c b/dlls/winewayland.drv/vulkan.c
--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/vulkan.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/vulkan.c
@@ -46,6 +46,7 @@
 {
     struct wayland_client_surface *ret = NULL;
     struct wayland_win_data *data;
+    BOOL preserve = process_name && !strcmp(process_name, "doometernalx64vk.exe");
 
     if (!(data = wayland_win_data_get(hwnd))) return NULL;
 
@@ -59,23 +60,30 @@
         client_surface_add_ref(&surface->client);
         data->stashed_client = surface;
     }
-    else if ((ret = data->stashed_client) && ReadAcquire(&ret->client.ref) == 1 &&
-             !ReadAcquire(&ret->client.busy_ref))
+    else if ((ret = data->stashed_client) && !ReadAcquire(&ret->client.busy_ref) &&
+             (ReadAcquire(&ret->client.ref) == 1 || preserve))
     {
         /* cannot decrease the ref count here as there is a
          * new VkSurface referencing this client surface */
         data->stashed_client = NULL;
-        /* detach the client surface to ensure it is reparented */
-        wayland_client_surface_attach(ret, NULL);
-        if (data->client_surface == ret)
+        /* DOOM retains old VkSurfaces after destroying their swapchains.
+         * Preserve its idle wl_surface and attachment so HDR replacements
+         * keep the compositor's DMA-BUF feedback and the last visible frame.
+         * Attachment updates still handle an actual parent/role change. */
+        if (!preserve)
         {
-            InterlockedExchange(&ret->client.presentation_owner, FALSE);
-            data->client_surface = NULL;
-        }
-        if (!list_empty(&ret->hwnd_entry))
-        {
-            list_remove(&ret->hwnd_entry);
-            list_init(&ret->hwnd_entry);
+            /* detach the client surface to ensure it is reparented */
+            wayland_client_surface_attach(ret, NULL);
+            if (data->client_surface == ret)
+            {
+                InterlockedExchange(&ret->client.presentation_owner, FALSE);
+                data->client_surface = NULL;
+            }
+            if (!list_empty(&ret->hwnd_entry))
+            {
+                list_remove(&ret->hwnd_entry);
+                list_init(&ret->hwnd_entry);
+            }
         }
     }
     else ret = NULL;

